 "notes": [
  "Breadboard bank naming follows the catalogue: bank 't' = rows a-e and bank 'b' = rows f-j. In the image the a-e rows and the power rails (tp/tn) are at the bottom, so those rails are named tp/tn.",
  "Column and rail hole numbers are estimated from pixel positions in the circuit image.",
  "Button legs sit in columns 4 and 6 across the centre gap. Side 1 (1.l/1.r) is column 4, which goes to 5V. Side 2 (2.l/2.r) is column 6, which goes to pin 2 and the resistor.",
  "The red wire goes to the + rail (tp). The black wire goes to the - rail (tn).",
  "The orange wire links column 4 to the + rail (5V). A black wire links the resistor's far column (9) to the - rail (GND).",
  "The Arduino GND wire is taken to be the second GND pin on the power header (GND.2).",
  "The manual's resistor is 10k ohm. It is set as value=10000."
